      likesYou: "said yes to you", likesYouTitle: "Said yes to you", likesYouNote: "Answer yes back and names and Telegram open.", likesYouBanner: "This person said yes to you. Answer yes and you both see the names and can write to each other.",
      likesTitle: "Tell me when someone answers me «yes»", likesText: "The bot messages you right away who answered you «yes» (nickname). At most once in 10 minutes.",
      abLink: "About the project and your data", abTitle: "About the project and data",
      ab1h: "What Kinkoverse is", ab1: "A non-commercial project, a sister project of the Kinkosmos site. No ads, no paid features. Data is never sold or handed to anyone.",
      ab2h: "What is kept", ab2: "Date of birth (others see an age group or the exact age — your choice), gender, nickname, «About», what you look for and who to show.\nChecklist answers — encrypted.\nA map area of about 1 km — the point itself is not kept.\nWhich connected chats you are in.\nYour Telegram id, @username and Telegram name — so that you can be written to after a mutual yes.\nYour «yes» and «not now», reports.",
      ab3h: "What is not kept", ab3: "Exact coordinates, conversations, group messages, photos.",
      ab4h: "Who sees what", ab4: "Neighbours from your chats (and from the Universe — checked chats approved by the owner — and from open space, if you switched them on): nickname, gender, age (a group or exact — the person's choice), role, rough distance, match percent, «About» (if open) and the checklist comparison (unless turned off).\nAfter a mutual yes: your Telegram name, exact age and a link to your profile.\nYour «yes» is seen right away — your nickname and card, without name or Telegram. Your «not now» is never shown.\nThe admin and moderators: profiles and answers for moderation, never your location. The admin also sees who you have a «yes» or a mutual yes with and who changed it — to sort out errors and reports. And a general people map: each person's rough zone (~5 km²) with the nickname — the bot keeps nothing finer than the zone. Every such view goes to the journal. The admin can open your Telegram account, moderators only if you were reported. Every such view goes to a journal.",
      ab5h: "Where it is kept", ab5: "On Cloudflare servers; the database is in the European Union.",
      ab6h: "How long", ab6: "If you do not open Kinkoverse for 2 months, your profile is hidden from the map. After 5 months the bot starts warning about deletion (three times, once a month); after 8 months the profile is deleted.\nThe admin's and moderators' view journal is kept for 180 days.",
      ab7h: "How to delete everything", ab7: "«Profile» → «Settings» → «Delete account». Everything is deleted at once. If a moderator blocked the account, only the block mark stays.",
      ab8h: "Contact", ab8: "A contact form will come later.",
      pCard: "My card", pSettings: "Settings", previewTitle: "How neighbours see you", previewNote: "Distance and percent differ for each.",
      digestTitle: "Weekly digest", digestText: "Once a week the bot tells you in the private chat how many new neighbours and mutual yes there are. Only if something is new.",
      digestAsk: "Get a weekly message in the chat with the bot about new neighbours and mutual yes?", digestYes: "Yes, send it", digestNo: "No, thanks",
      filtersOffNote: "Test mode: the admin has switched gender and age filters off — everyone from your chats and space is shown.",
      bkTitle: "Backup", bkWhere: "All data is in the Cloudflare D1 database (in the EU). Cloudflare keeps its own history of the last days — roll back in GitHub: Actions → «restore database». This button also makes a file you keep.",
